<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Admin | {{#isNew}}New Infobox Template{{/isNew}}{{^isNew}}Edit Infobox Template{{/isNew}} | {{siteName}}</title>
    {{>partials/head-deps.hbs}}
    {{>partials/head-styles.hbs}}
</head>
<body>
{{>partials/admin-shell.hbs}}
    <h1>{{#isNew}}New Infobox Template{{/isNew}}{{^isNew}}Edit Infobox Template{{/isNew}}</h1>
    {{#error}}<div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">{{error}}</div>{{/error}}
    {{! ib-form widens the form past the admin default so the field editor's rows and card preview fit
        side by side; the identity inputs above it keep the normal width of their own accord. }}
    <form method="post" action="{{#isNew}}/a/infoboxes{{/isNew}}{{^isNew}}/a/infoboxes/{{id}}{{/isNew}}" class="edit-form ib-form">
        {{{csrfField}}}
        <div class="mb-3" style="max-width:32rem">
            <label for="infoboxName" class="form-label">Name</label>
            <input class="form-control" type="text" name="name" id="infoboxName" value="{{name}}" placeholder="e.g. City Info" required>
            <p class="form-text">Shown as the infobox card's heading on the page.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3" style="max-width:32rem">
            <label for="slug" class="form-label">Slug</label>
            <input class="form-control" type="text" name="slug" value="{{slug}}" placeholder="e.g. app_info" id="slug">
            <p class="form-text">Stable identifier (lowercase letters, numbers, <code>-</code>, <code>_</code>). Leave blank to derive from name.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3" style="max-width:32rem">
            <label for="description" class="form-label">Description</label>
            <input class="form-control" type="text" name="description" value="{{description}}" placeholder="Optional note for editors" id="description">
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <label class="form-label">Fields</label>
            {{! Visual field editor. Revealed by wk-infobox-editor.js, which keeps the textarea below in
                sync as the authoritative form value — so with JS off (or via "Edit Source") the plain
                text format is still the whole story. Same arrangement as the navigation menu editor. }}
            <div id="infoboxFieldEditor" class="ib-editor" hidden>
                <div class="ib-ed-bar">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-add><i class="mdi mdi-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> Add field</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" data-add-heading title="Group the fields below it under a subheading on the card"><i class="mdi mdi-format-header-pound" aria-hidden="true"></i> Add section</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-link ms-auto" data-toggle-source><i class="mdi mdi-code-tags" aria-hidden="true"></i> Edit Source</button>
                </div>
                <div class="ib-ed-main">
                    <div class="ib-ed-rows" data-rows></div>
                    <div class="ib-ed-preview">
                        <p class="ib-ed-preview-label">Card preview</p>
                        <aside class="page-card wk-infobox ib-ed-preview-card">
                            <p class="page-toc-title wk-infobox-title" data-preview-title>Infobox</p>
                            <div data-preview></div>
                        </aside>
                        <p class="form-text mt-2 mb-0">Above is a sample rendering with stand-in values to simulate what a reader would see. (NOTE: on a real page a blank field is dropped, and a section with every field left blank is dropped along with its heading.)</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <textarea class="form-control font-monospace" name="fields" id="infoboxFields" aria-label="Infobox fields (source)" rows="8" placeholder="population | Population | string | | Residents at the most recent census.&#10;climate | Climate | enum | Tropical, Temperate, Arid | Köppen climate group.&#10;languages | Languages | multi | English, French, Spanish | Every language with official status here.&#10;capital | Capital city | boolean | | Whether this is the country's seat of government.">{{fieldsText}}</textarea>
            <details id="infoboxSyntaxHelp" class="form-text">
                <summary>Field syntax</summary>
                <p class="mb-1 mt-1">One field per line, columns divided by <code>|</code>. Only trailing columns may be left off.</p>
                <p class="mb-2 font-monospace">name | label | type | options | help</p>
                <ul class="mb-2">
                    <li><strong>name</strong>: required. The key the value is stored under; readers never see it.</li>
                    <li><strong>label</strong>: the caption on the card (defaults to the name).</li>
                    <li><strong>type</strong>: one of the four below. Append <code>*</code> (e.g. <code>enum*</code>) to mark the field required.</li>
                    <li><strong>options</strong>: the choices, comma-separated. <em>Required</em> for <code>enum</code> and <code>multi</code>, which have nothing to offer without it; ignored by the other two.</li>
                    <li><strong>help</strong>: what the field means, in a sentence. Shown to editors under the input <em>and</em> to readers: on the page the label picks up a dotted underline that reveals this on hover or tap. Worth filling in wherever a label alone could be read two ways.</li>
                </ul>
                <table class="table table-sm align-middle mb-2">
                    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Allowed values</th><th>Shown on page as...</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>string</code></td>
                            <td>any text</td>
                            <td>the text, with inline Markdown (bold, italic, links) applied</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>enum</code></td>
                            <td>one option from the dropdown (or none)</td>
                            <td>the selected option</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>multi</code></td>
                            <td>any number of items from the list (or none)</td>
                            <td>the selected options, each in its own capsule</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>boolean</code></td>
                            <td>yes or no from the dropdown (or neither)</td>
                            <td>a green "Yes" or a gray "No"</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <p class="mb-2">Start a line with <code>#</code> to make a section heading, e.g. <code># Geography</code> (logically group items under it).</p>
                <p class="mb-0"><code>enum</code> and <code>multi</code> offer the choices specified in the "options" column and differ only in how many of them an editor may pick.</p>
            </details>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary" href="/a/infoboxes">Cancel</a>
    </form>
    {{^isNew}}
    <form method="post" action="/a/infoboxes/{{id}}/delete" class="mt-4" onsubmit="return confirm('Delete this template and its path rules? Pages keep their stored data but stop showing the infobox.');">
        {{{csrfField}}}
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger">Delete template</button>
    </form>
    {{/isNew}}
{{>partials/admin-shell-end.hbs}}
<script src="/static/wk-infobox-editor.js?v={{assetVersion}}"></script>
{{{bodyHtml}}}</body>
</html>
